=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: moving errexit from the shebang to the long form makes the script stricter
origin: a false positive this project shipped in v0.1.8 and an audit
origin2: reproduced: `#!/bin/sh -e` -> `#!/bin/sh` + `set -o errexit` blocked
origin3: at high saying "a failing command no longer fails the script", over a
origin4: script that was measured still exiting 1 on a failing test. Refusing
origin5: to read a spelling is not the same as that spelling being absent, and
origin6: printing the second when you mean the first is a false statement in a
origin7: blocking message.
=== before: scripts/test.sh ===
#!/bin/sh -e

pytest -q
=== after: scripts/test.sh ===
#!/bin/sh
set -o errexit
set -o nounset

pytest -q
